"""gdocs: read, edit and verify Google Docs (Chief tool pack `gdocs`).

Two routes, picked per call:

* api      GDOCS_TOKEN holds an OAuth access token with a Drive scope: Drive v3
           export (read), HTML upload with conversion (replace-outline) and
           comments.create (comment). No browser.
* browser  The person's own Google session in a cmux browser tab, no token:
           read = same-origin fetch of /document/d/ID/mobilebasic (the export
           URL redirects to another origin, so a page fetch cannot read it);
           write = a synthetic ClipboardEvent('paste') of HTML on the editor's
           event target (iframe.docs-texteventtarget-iframe), plus synthetic
           keydown events on that same element for select-all, caret moves,
           find (Cmd+F), comments (Cmd+Option+M) and suggesting mode. Docs
           ignores real keys sent to a background tab and accepts these.

Every write reads the doc back and compares outlines (verify); exit 1 on a
mismatch. Offline helpers (`md2html`, `parse-html`, `verify --html`) need no
network and back the tests in tests/toolpack_gdocs.rs.

plans/cmux-next/chief-gdocs-DESIGN.md has the design and the measurements.
"""

